We can find that $\angle ADE = \angle AED = 70^\circ$ (isosceles triangle) and $\angle DEC = 2 \angle AED = 140^\circ$.  Likewise, $\triangle BEC$ is an isosceles triangle as well, with one angle $\angle BEC = 180 - \angle DEC = 40^\circ$.  Then we can see that $\angle AEB = \angle AED - \∠ BEC = 30^\circ$.

Finally, $\angle AEB = \angle AEC = 180 - \angle BEC = 40^\circ$.  Since $\angle AEC = 40$ DEG, then $\angle AEC = 40$ DEG (isosceles triangle), which gives us $\angle EBC = (180-40) / 2 = \boxed{70}$ DEG. </think> <answer> 70 </answer>

